{"availability":"available","full":"yang-ai-lab/Inertia-1","name":"Inertia-1","description":"[NeurIPS 2026] Inertia-1: An Open Exploration of Wearable Motion Foundation Models","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":39,"forks":2,"created":"2026-06-08T06:32:41Z","updated":"2026-09-28T23:12:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://yang-ai-lab.github.io/Inertia-1/","topics":["accelerometer","foundation-models","healthcare-ai","time-series","time-series-foundation-models","wearable-ai","wearable-health"],"demo":"https://yang-ai-lab.github.io/Inertia-1/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T12:59:51.458Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T12:59:51.458Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T12:59:51.458Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T12:59:51.458Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:30:33.123Z","stars":35,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-09T08:55:31.374Z","stars":36,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-10T12:59:51.458Z","stars":39,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Inertia-1 is an open exploration of wearable motion foundation models. Motion sensing is fragmented — datasets disagree on sampling rate, window length, sensor modality, body placement, and even signal format, and nearly every task gets its own bespoke model. Inertia-1 studies the full lifecycle of motion models (data, sensing, objectives, and scale) inside a single, controlled space, asking whether one self-supervised representation learned from raw accelerometry can transfer across the body, devices, and downstream tasks."],"features":["Self-supervised pretraining on raw accelerometry, with the key exploration axes exposed as first-class knobs (uniaxial vs. triaxial, sampling rate, window length).","Downstream evaluation on human-activity-recognition (HAR) and freezing-of-gait (FoG) datasets via linear probing / full finetuning.","Patient-level disease & medication detection via attention-based multiple-instance learning (MIL) on frozen embeddings."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yang-ai-lab/Inertia-1/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a2f1bab59c11a86770ab06c0d144322978c2ab73b07452a548d95fc49ddfd1d7","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:30:33.123Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T12:59:51.458Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Inertia-1 is an open exploration of wearable motion foundation models. Motion sensing is fragmented — datasets disagree on sampling rate, window length, sensor modality, body placement, and even signal format, and nearly every task gets its own bespoke model. Inertia-1 studies the full lifecycle of motion models (data, sensing, objectives, and scale) inside a single, controlled space, asking whether one self-supervised representation learned from raw accelerometry can transfer across the body, devices, and downstream tasks.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yang-ai-lab/Inertia-1/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a2f1bab59c11a86770ab06c0d144322978c2ab73b07452a548d95fc49ddfd1d7","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yang-ai-lab/Inertia-1/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T12:59:51.458Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-28T23:12:23Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/yang-ai-lab/Inertia-1/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T12:59:51.458Z","hash":"a2f1bab59c11a86770ab06c0d144322978c2ab73b07452a548d95fc49ddfd1d7","originalBytes":8814,"storedBytes":8814,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["data","fog","pretrain","har","motion","scripts","eval","preprocessing","split","bash","disease","nhanes","config","frozen","detection","downstream","inertia-1","mil","patchtst","patient","python","dataset","datasets","exploration","inertia1","license","models","own","pretraining","probe","root","evaluation","layout","linear","parquet","placeholder","raw","splits","transformer","window","windows","accelerometer","axes","bag","download","e.g.","foundation","g